        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Carrhae</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">9 June 53 BCE, the date given by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ovid">Ovid</a> in Book 6 of the Fasti</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Near the ancient town of Carrhae, present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harran">Harran</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, on the plain of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-licinius-crassus">Marcus Licinius Crassus</a>, with seven legions of about 28,000 to 35,000 heavy infantry, about 4,000 light infantry and 4,000 cavalry according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plutarch">Plutarch</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire</a> under the spahbod <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/surena">Surena</a>, with roughly 10,000 men</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-licinius-crassus">Crassus</a> was killed when truce negotiations turned violent. Most of his army was killed or captured; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plutarch">Plutarch</a> gives about 20,000 killed and 10,000 captured, and Parthian casualties as minimal.</span></div>
        </div>
