    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/surena">Surena</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horse-archer">horse archers</a> stayed out of reach of the Roman javelins, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>' close formations could not drive them off or fight back, while his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cataphract">cataphracts</a> charged whenever the Romans loosened their ranks.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-licinius-crassus">Crassus</a> refused Artavasdes II's offer of a route through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> and of reinforcements, and marched straight through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/surena">Surena</a>, whose force was heavily outnumbered, had been sent only to scout and harass him.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plutarch">Plutarch</a> gives about 20,000 Roman dead and 10,000 prisoners. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-cassius-longinus">Gaius Cassius Longinus</a> led about 10,000 survivors back to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and defended the province against Parthian attacks.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthians</a> kept up their supply of arrows by using thousands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">camels</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-licinius-crassus">Crassus</a> had hoped would run out before his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">legionaries</a> gave way.</p></aside>
    </section>

